    @*         <td >@item.Price.ToString("C2")</td> *@
    @*     </tr> *@
    @* } *@
    </tbody>
</table>


 <div class="mt-3 question-box">
                Frequently Asked Questions after submission 
                
                <h3 class="mt-2">What happens next?</h3>
                <p> If you’ve added a digital file to your project, you’re all set! If not, please visit [My Projects] to upload or link a digital file, or mail a hard copy to the festival by the entry deadline. Please check the festival submission guidelines 
                </p>
               <h3  class="mt-2"> When will I find out if my project is selected?</h3>
               <p> You can check the current status of all your submissions on your [Submissions] page. 
                The festival is responsible to inform you and you may contact the festivals support for that.
                </p>
                <h3  class="mt-2">Can I update or make changes to my project file?</h3>
                <p>Yes, you can update your digital project file anytime. Simply go to [My Projects] to manage your project file.
                But keep in touch with festival and let they know about your changes, because they may exported your submissions information. 
                </p>
                <h3  class="mt-2">Can I withdraw my project from a festival?</h3>
               <p> Yes, you can withdraw your project from a festival at any time. Visit [Submissions](#) and click on Withdraw. Please note that withdrawing does not automatically issue a refund, and you must let festival know about it personally. 
                The festival will only loose their access to your project page in Hisubmit website. 
                </p>
                <h3  class="mt-2">What is the refund policy?</h3>
               <p> Refunds are handled at the discretion of the festivals to which you’ve submitted. Please contact the festival directly if you have a refund request.
                </p>
                <h3  class="mt-2">What is the submission platform's duty regarding my artwork file?</h3>
               <p> The submission platform has no duty regarding the artwork copyright  submitted by the artist to the contest. The responsibility for the project remains with the artist.
                </p>
                <h3  class="mt-2">How do I reach customer service?</h3>
                <p> For questions about a festival, we recommend contacting the festival directly. You can also reach Hisubmit Support at [support@hisubmit.com]. We’re happy to help!
                </p>
            </div>
</body>
</html>
